<article class="env-lemma" id="0G8B">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G8B">Lemma <span data-tag="0G8B">50.23.8</span>.</a> Let $X \to S$ and $i : Z \to X$ be as in Lemma <a href="/tag/0G86" data-tag="0G86">50.23.3</a>. Assume $X \to S$ is smooth and $Z \to X$ Koszul regular. The Gysin maps $\gamma ^{p, q}$ are compatible with the de Rham differentials on $\Omega ^\bullet _{X/S}$ and $\Omega ^\bullet _{Z/S}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows immediately from Lemma <a href="/tag/0G87" data-tag="0G87">50.23.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>